From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 16:47:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08121/11362] [outer-loop] Gate the win-transition supply
 default-OFF; correct both artifacts after adversarial review

THE DECISION. The 2026-08-01 win-transition supply shipped LIVE and UNFLAGGED on the scored
path. Its effect is UNMEASURED -- not measured-null -- because across 128 live induce calls the
argument was DELIVERED to the changed call site 0 times. With 0 delivered calls a live A/B has 0
discordant pairs, so an exact paired test's smallest reachable two-sided p is 1.0: unfalsifiable,
not underpowered. Under the standing default-OFF discipline, unmeasured is sufficient on its own.
It is now behind CARNOT_ARC_SUPPLY_WIN_TRANSITION, default 0.

OFF omits the keyword ENTIRELY rather than passing None -- both compute the same thing for the
shipped proposer, but omitting is what the pre-change call actually did. Verified end-to-end on
the live path in both directions: with the flag OFF the keyword is absent even in the case where
the ungated code WOULD have delivered it, and with it ON the agent's own level-up row arrives at
the gated call site. Trajectory identical (vc33 levels=2 actions=387) in all six runs, so the
gate is inert on behaviour, as a default-OFF gate must be. 18 assertions, both directions.

Turning it ON today buys almost nothing: with the flag ON the shipped arm still delivers 0,
because every available call routes into execute_bounded_llm_reinduction, whose _call_induce has
no win_transition parameter at all.

BOTH ARTIFACTS CORRECTED. Two independent adversarial reviews returned 17 required corrections
between them. Every one was RE-VERIFIED against the runs' own cells before being applied -- a
reviewer in this session had already been wrong once. All 17 survived. Never-prune throughout:
no prior number is deleted, each correction sits beside the figure it corrects, and both original
honest_verdict strings are preserved byte-for-byte (moved out of the honest_verdict slot only
because summarize_artifact.py reads that field first, and a superseded claim there would make
the correction decorative).

EXPOSURE (holds=true, 9 corrections). The strongest: the claim that the routing predicate and
the availability predicate are "the same predicate in practice" is FALSE as a statement about
the code. next_level_episode additionally requires _previous_level_complete_grid is not None,
set from a guarded extraction that can fail, while _win_transition is set unconditionally. I ran
my own counterexample -- null only that field on vc33/400 and delivery goes 0 -> 1 at the gated
site with the trajectory unchanged. So the zero is EMPIRICAL and contingent on
win_state_exemplar_captured holding 30/30, not structural. Also: the headline double-counted 3
bit-identical A/A control cells (de-duplicated 124 calls / 28 available / 22.6%); the single
shipped configuration is 28 calls / 4 available / 14.3% with 22 of 25 games at exactly zero; the
clustered mean is 15.9% not 15.7%; availability was measured with solve-registry-derived routing
in the loop, so it is an UPPER bound on a hidden game's.

G50T (holds=FALSE -- the existence claim survives, the CAUSE does not). I rebuilt the per-node
join the shipped probe never computed. Residual pairs by debit class: {partial 10, fully-probed
8, never-probed 1}. The never-probed class the mis-debiting story is about is the LEAST likely
to hold residual work (7.7% vs 23.1% for fully-probed). Decisively, CONTROL runs the same defect
at the same intensity (411/698 = 58.9% executed where debited vs defer 162/280 = 57.9%) with
MORE never-probed nodes (17 vs 13), and neither exhausts nor leaves any residual. Root-cause
proportionality is also inverted in the original: the HUD mask collapses 596 observed frames
into 56 nodes and the guard attributes 214 of 215 branchings to in-mask differences against 1
outside, so mask-induced aliasing dominates the 90/783 raw aliasing the artifact led with. q3 is
0.6083 not 0.633. Effective evidence is one distinct run per (game, arm): control_b is
byte-identical to control on 75/75 and all three seeds are byte-identical within every arm.

g50t is SCOPED, NOT FIXED -- a frontier-correctness fix deserves its own measured change.

FRESHNESS ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS (13 artifacts, provenance-only). Editing arc_competition_agent.py
invalidates the hash-pinned freshness chain, so the next link is appended to each affected
artifact. The evidence is measured, not argued: the delta can only matter if _win_transition was
ever non-None where HEAD passed it, and it was None on all 98 of the 128 live induce calls that
reached the site, so passing None and omitting the keyword are the same computation. A rebuild
was tried first on outer_loop_arc_reset_charge_attribution and REVERTED byte-for-byte -- it moved
published figures from a week of unrelated drift, which is not mine to own. Every one of the 13
edits was mechanically verified to touch `provenance` and nothing else.

